<title>JAPAN: Japan March rubber imports up 26.3 pct yr/yr-MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March rubber imports up 26.3 pct yr/yr-MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's rubber imports in March totalled 77,843 tonnes, up 26.3 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			Mar 97	 Feb 97	Mar 96</p>
<p> Total		77,843	 62,135	61,611</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand	   58,833	 48,990	48,224</p>
<p> Indonesia	  12,881	  7,270	 9,486</p>
<p> Malaysia	    4,306	  4,577	 2,508</p>
<p>Total imports in the first three months of calendar 1997 were 203,899 tonnes against 191,102 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
